<title>JAPAN: M'bishi Heavy to build chemical plant in Indonesia.</title>
<headline>M'bishi Heavy to build chemical plant in Indonesia.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd said on Tuesday that it had received a turnkey order for a styrene monomer plant from P.T. Sytrindo Mono Indonesia.</p>
<p>The plant, with a production capacity of 200,000 tonnes per year, would be completed in June 1999, Mitsubishi Heavy said in a statement.</p>
<p>A company spokesman declined to comment on the value of the order.</p>
<p>Styrene monomer is used to make synthetic rubber and polystyrene used in products such as electric appliances.</p>
</text>
